1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,177
This video shows how to build a subject flow:

2
00:00:04,177 --> 00:00:10,034
the actions that run when an agent, or the AI, completes an activity with a disposition.

3
00:00:10,034 --> 00:00:14,769
It covers the Finish, Try Again and New Activity actions, and what the

4
00:00:14,769 --> 00:00:16,700
Convert Lead action adds.

5
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:25,546
When a call ends, somebody has to decide what happens next.

6
00:00:25,546 --> 00:00:30,250
Try again tomorrow, book a follow-up, or stop calling this person.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,715
A subject flow puts that decision in one place.

8
00:00:34,715 --> 00:00:38,010
Each disposition has one or more actions.

9
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:43,564
So agents only pick the outcome, and the follow-up work is created for

10
00:00:43,564 --> 00:00:45,840
them, the same way every time.

11
00:00:50,031 --> 00:00:56,676
Open Interaction Center, Management, Subject Flows, and click Manage Flow next to the subject.

12
00:00:56,676 --> 00:00:58,404
A new flow is empty.

13
00:00:58,404 --> 00:01:01,195
Click Add Action, and pick the type:

14
00:01:01,195 --> 00:01:06,711
Finish, Try Again, New Activity, or Convert Lead, which appears with the CRM.

15
00:01:07,162 --> 00:01:10,782
Finish completes the activity and nothing else happens.

16
00:01:10,782 --> 00:01:14,520
Pick the disposition it responds to, here Not Interested.

17
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:19,741
When to choose this disposition is guidance the AI reads when it picks an outcome.

18
00:01:19,741 --> 00:01:22,886
It starts as the disposition's own description.

19
00:01:22,886 --> 00:01:28,107
Show communication preferences lets the action flag the contact, here Do not call,

20
00:01:28,107 --> 00:01:31,015
and with the CRM, set the status of a lead.

21
00:01:31,015 --> 00:01:32,142
Click Create.

22
00:01:36,349 --> 00:01:40,943
Try Again creates a new try of the same activity, with the attempt

23
00:01:40,943 --> 00:01:42,602
count raised by one.

24
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:47,579
Pick No Answer, and set the maximum attempts, here three tries in total.

25
00:01:48,029 --> 00:01:53,667
The assignment type keeps the same owner, or gives the follow-up to a specific user.

26
00:01:53,667 --> 00:01:58,678
Default schedule hours says how many hours later it is scheduled, here 24.

27
00:01:58,678 --> 00:02:02,249
The agent can change the date on the Complete page.

28
00:02:02,249 --> 00:02:03,439
Click Create.

29
00:02:07,646 --> 00:02:12,588
New Activity creates a new activity, for the same subject or another one.

30
00:02:12,588 --> 00:02:17,155
Pick Interested, and the target subject, here Test Drive Follow-up.

31
00:02:17,155 --> 00:02:22,786
The new activity takes its campaign, channel and interaction type from that subject.

32
00:02:23,236 --> 00:02:27,701
Set its urgency, and the hours until it is scheduled, here 48.

33
00:02:27,701 --> 00:02:33,676
A disposition can have several actions, for example Finish and New Activity together.

34
00:02:34,127 --> 00:02:39,547
Back in the list, the Missing flow badge is gone, because the subject now has actions.

35
00:02:43,739 --> 00:02:48,068
With the CRM on, Convert Lead converts a lead when an activity ends

36
00:02:48,068 --> 00:02:49,966
with a chosen disposition.

37
00:02:49,966 --> 00:02:56,134
It chooses the account, whether to create an opportunity, and what happens to the open activities.

38
00:02:56,134 --> 00:03:00,879
It runs before the other actions, so a follow-up lands on the new contact.

39
00:03:05,079 --> 00:03:09,418
When the agent picks a disposition on the Complete page, a preview lists

40
00:03:09,418 --> 00:03:11,199
the actions that will run.

41
00:03:11,949 --> 00:03:16,651
Each follow-up shows a Schedule at date and Preparation notes, which become the

42
00:03:16,651 --> 00:03:18,809
instructions of the new activity.

43
00:03:19,559 --> 00:03:24,946
If you change the flow, activities already scheduled keep working, and new completions

44
00:03:24,946 --> 00:03:26,469
use the new actions.

45
00:03:30,669 --> 00:03:34,629
Retry unanswered calls a few times, then stop.

46
00:03:35,379 --> 00:03:39,149
Book a follow-up automatically when a customer is interested.

47
00:03:39,899 --> 00:03:43,019
Stop calling people who say they are not interested.

48
00:03:43,769 --> 00:03:46,629
Convert a lead the moment it qualifies.

49
00:03:48,629 --> 00:03:53,026
Give every disposition an action, and the next step happens by itself.

50
00:03:53,026 --> 00:03:57,424
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

51
00:03:57,424 --> 00:03:58,929
Thanks for watching.

